%% On-Edge V8: one robot trial end to end (v8-demo-robot / v8-robot-pilot procedure, onedge_v8 0.1.3).
%% Drawn from firmware/trust_monitor_v8, v8/onedge_v8/runner.py and the URI integration on 2026-09-29.
%% Timings marked "measured" are bench-pilot or demo observations, not guarantees.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor OP as Operator (pendant + dashboard)
    participant DB as Dashboard (browser)
    participant RN as Pi daemon (runner + recorder)
    participant NANO as Nano 33 BLE trust monitor
    participant OPTO as Optocoupler (D12 to SI0 and SI1)
    participant DRV as UR ROS 2 driver (Pi, localhost-only)
    participant UR as UR5 CB3 controller

    Note over RN,UR: Always on: /joint_states 125 Hz (fresh or stale, never zero-filled). Safety mode and program state are latched topics
    DRV-->>RN: joint_states, safety_mode, robot_program_running

    rect rgba(128,128,128,0.08)
    Note over OP,RN: Session start (once)
    OP->>DB: Start campaign (matrix reviewed, robot motion authorized)
    DB->>RN: POST campaign/start (plan hash)
    RN->>RN: open session, record plan, config, git commit and source hashes
    end

    RN-->>DB: AWAITING_CONFIRMATION (next trial)
    OP->>DB: Start T00x
    DB->>RN: POST campaign/confirm

    rect rgba(128,128,128,0.08)
    Note over RN,UR: Preconditions
    RN->>RN: joint telemetry fresh? safety mode not a fault?
    opt a trajectory goal from an earlier attempt is still active
        RN->>DRV: cancel goal (before D12 is raised, or the paused sweep would resume)
    end
    end

    rect rgba(128,128,128,0.08)
    Note over RN,UR: Arm the monitor
    RN->>NANO: CONFIG {workload ECC or ZKP, alpha}
    NANO->>NANO: trust = 100, cycle = 0, attack flag cleared
    NANO->>OPTO: D12 HIGH
    OPTO->>UR: 24 V on SI0 and SI1 (safeguard loop closed)
    NANO-->>RN: cfg record (+ out record if D12 changed)
    UR-->>DRV: safety mode NORMAL
    DRV-->>RN: safety_mode NORMAL
    opt program not running
        OP->>UR: Play (External Control)
    end
    RN->>DRV: switch_controller: activate passthrough_trajectory_controller
    end

    rect rgba(128,128,128,0.08)
    Note over RN,UR: Motion
    RN->>DRV: FollowJointTrajectory phase 1 (approach to Pick, 5 s)
    DRV->>UR: trajectory via External Control (ports 50001 to 50004)
    UR-->>DRV: executed
    DRV-->>RN: phase 1 succeeded
    RN->>RN: settle: all joints below 0.01 rad/s for 250 ms, no gap over 40 ms
    RN->>DRV: FollowJointTrajectory phase 2 (sweep Pick, Transfer, Place, Transfer, Pick, 10 s)
    DRV->>UR: trajectory
    RN->>RN: confirm moving on fresh telemetry (at least 0.05 rad/s for 100 ms)
    end

    loop every workload cycle (measured about 121 ms ECC, 233 ms ZKP, device clock rate-corrected)
        NANO->>NANO: read commands (only between cycles)
        NANO->>NANO: workload: ECC key generation or two scalar multiplications (DWT timed)
        NANO->>NANO: obs = 0 if attack flag else 100 minus any execution-time penalty
        NANO->>NANO: trust = alpha x obs + (1 - alpha) x trust
        NANO-->>RN: upd record (seq, t_us, t0_us, exec_ms, obs, trust, d12, pw_us)
    end

    alt sustained failure (injected failure longer than the updates needed to cross)
        RN->>NANO: ATTACK (800 ms after moving confirmed, plus seeded jitter)
        Note over NANO: waits for the current cycle to end (measured 0 to 1 cycle)
        NANO-->>RN: cmd record ATTACK processed
        Note over NANO: n zero-observation updates: alpha 0.5 needs 2, 0.3 needs 4, 0.1 needs 12
        NANO->>NANO: update with trust below 30
        NANO->>OPTO: D12 LOW (same cycle, measured about 10 us after the crossing update)
        NANO-->>RN: upd (below = 1) and out (level 0) records
        OPTO->>UR: SI0 and SI1 open
        UR->>UR: Category 2 safeguard stop: controlled deceleration, hold, sweep goal PAUSED (not ended)
        UR-->>DRV: safety mode SAFEGUARD_STOP
        DRV-->>RN: safety_mode SAFEGUARD_STOP (measured about 16 to 21 ms after the D12-low command, aligned clocks)
        RN->>NANO: RECOVER (after the failure window)
        NANO->>NANO: attack flag cleared, trust climbs back, D12 stays LOW (latched until the next CONFIG)
        RN->>RN: wait for the telemetry standstill criterion, record the held stop
        RN->>DRV: cancel the paused sweep goal while D12 is still LOW
        DRV-->>RN: goal canceled
    else brief failure (RECOVER processed before the crossing update)
        RN->>NANO: ATTACK, then RECOVER after the failure window
        NANO->>NANO: trust dips, stays at or above 30, D12 stays HIGH
        UR-->>DRV: sweep executed
        DRV-->>RN: phase 2 succeeded
    else no-injection control
        Note over RN,NANO: no ATTACK or RECOVER, trust stays at 100
        UR-->>DRV: sweep executed
        DRV-->>RN: phase 2 succeeded
    end

    RN->>RN: attempt summary: device-clock intervals, clock fit (rate-corrected), outcome, quality
    RN-->>DB: trial result, next trial awaits confirmation
    Note over NANO,UR: The next trial's CONFIG raises D12 again, which clears the safeguard stop
